    "body": "Judgement calls for the maintainer (in full in docs/decisions/369-lathe-holder-body.md):\n1. **One `ToolBody` component carries its frame** (spindle or lathe), rather than a separate lathe component. Undo of a tool delete, the file and the stamp follow for free.\n2. **The excluded insert zone is the tool's modelled footprint swept so far.** A fixed insert radius or crediting the whole pass was rejected, because either could hide a holder leading into uncut stock. A mesh that includes the insert plate can over-report; the follow-up is #396.\n3. **\"Holder not judged\" is a non-blocking path note** on bodiless turning tools. No CL or post golden changed.\n4. **A lathe body on a Bore used by a milling op refuses generation by name.** No milling law reads a lathe frame.\n5. **Performance:** the judge's work grows with instants × band runs. That is fine for test meshes, but a large vendor body over a long path may be slow in debug builds.",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
